Z||000000||8Ball||08-26-2001||12:10 AM||||I have been driving my car very little to make sure the work I have done to it has gone well. But I have started to hear and feel a loud pop every once in a while under the drivers seat. Only thing I can think of is maybe an air bubble in the coolant system<BR>or maybe the water boiling in the coolent tube just under the seat?<P>Does this sound right to anyone?<BR>I do know I have to work on the coolant system. It nearly overheated this last time I drove it and I have to try to figure out why.||||reg||5
Z||000001||starfighter007@msn.com||08-26-2001||12:31 AM||||Yeah I guess if you have a over heating problem and you think that the noise you hear is coming from under the seat You might want to check and see if the coolant tube is not crushed ||||reg||1
