Z||000003||Mach10||08-26-2001||12:53 PM||||Could be an air bubble zippin' around in there. I'd burp it a few times, and see if that helps...||||reg||7
Z||000004||dgroves||08-26-2001||02:44 PM||||Have just gone through a bunch of work to solve an overheating problem with my '86GT. In the end the main problem turned out to be leaking pressure caps on both ends of the system. Cheap parts but easy to overlook when troubleshooting. The main clue is coolant loss. I thought something else was wrong and the coolant was boiling out when it got hot. NOT! The coolant was leaking when engine got to temp and pressure and then without adequate volumn the temp would skyrocket.||||reg||1
Z||000005||fiero56||08-26-2001||03:24 PM||||I've heard eating certain food types the nght before can cause similar symptoms.||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||08-26-2001||07:24 PM||||any time or durring/after a turn?<P>The seat hardware often moves slightly around turns. this is common. make sure all the seat bolts are tight. It won't eliminate it but should reduce it.||||reg||1
